              DIGITAL PARTNERS WITH MICROSOFT TO LAUNCH
              MICROSOFT'S WINDOWS 95 INTERNET HOME PAGE


            Digital Prioris PC Servers Power Key Web Site


MAYNARD, Mass. -- August 17, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that its Prioris HX 590DP PC server has been chosen 
by Microsoft as the power behind its Windows 95 home page.  
Building on Digital's and Microsoft's recent alliance to meet 
customer demand for Microsoft solutions in true enterprise-wide 
computing environments, Digital is proud to provide the hardware and 
service necessary to support the largest on-line event in Internet 
history.  Microsoft's Windows 95 home page is located on the World 
Wide Web at http://www.windows.microsoft.com.  The Windows 95 online 
launch event begins August 24, 1995.

     This partnership will allow large volumes of Internet users 
easy and fast access to the new Windows 95 home page and underscores 
Digital's continued leadership in networking, enterprise computing, 
service, support and systems integration.  In addition to extensive 
Microsoft information, the Windows 95 online "Product Pavilion" will 
feature a hot link to Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit home 
page (scheduled to go "live" on August 24 at http://www.pc.digital.
com), as well as information on the Digital Prioris HX 590DP system.  
Digital's Prioris PC servers will be featured in an "About This Web 
Site" section of the Windows 95 site.  

     In addition, Digital and Microsoft will kick off a "Win this 
Web Server" giveaway, as a prize to a selected site visitor randomly 
chosen from those who fill out the online event "Guest Book" (site 
visitors from those locations where such a giveaway is prohibited by 
law will be ineligible).

     "In addition to its history of leadership in online technology,
Digital intends to lead in Internet web servers by capitalizing on 
its PC server and networking capabilities," said Duane Dickhut, vice 
president of Digital's PC Server Product Line.  "By virtue of this 
leadership, Digital has been selected by the largest software 
company in the world as a key partner to assist in the launch of 
Windows 95 through one of the greatest online events in Internet 
history."

     Microsoft will celebrate the retail availability of Windows 95 
on August 24 with a limited-attendance customer event at the 
company's Redmond, Wash., campus and through the online launch 
event.  Given the key role Internet access will play, not only in 
the Windows 95 launch but also in providing users with on-going 
information and support beyond August 24, server power and 
reliability is critical.  Digital is supplying 10 servers to 
Microsoft to support the site, with the servers located in cities 
around the world to balance network traffic for different 
geographies.  Other software and hardware companies also will 
participate at the Redmond launch event, demonstrating new products 
that take advantage of Windows 95 innovations. The event will be 
downlinked via satellite to more than 40 cities across the United 
States.  

     "Digital's legacy of Internet expertise and PC server 
experience made it the logical company to partner with for this 
historic event," said Joachim Kempin, senior vice president of 
Microsoft Corporation's OEM division. "This partnership builds on 
our long-standing alliance with Digital to bring first Windows NT - 
and now Windows 95 - to the enterprise computing environment." 

     High-quality servers are the foundation of a successful home 
page, ensuring availability and handling high volumes of user 
access.  Digital's Prioris HX 590 system is a superior departmental 
application server for workgroups numbering in the hundreds.  The 
Prioris HX 590 is optimized to meet customers' needs both today and 
in the future, with processor, disk and memory scalability.  
Specifically designed for expansion, growth and longevity, Prioris 
HX systems deliver excellent reliability and fault-tolerant 
features, such as:

     _	Hot-swap drive support;
     _	PCI I/O technology providing 132 Mb/s throughput;
     _	Symmetric multiprocessing;
     _	Support for Digital's RAID controller, for internal and 
        external SCSI support;
     _	512KB write-back cache standard;
     _	Error Correction Code (ECC) memory support up to 256MB, to 
        guard against data corruption;
     _	A second 450 watt redundant power supply (optional) 
        supporting automatic failover and current sharing;
     _	Redundant cooling system with failover fans; and
     _	Dual-channel hot-swap backplane for increased redundancy.

     Prioris servers are covered by a three-year, limited warranty, 
that provides next-day on-site response to a majority of users from 
Digital's Multivendor Customer Services organization or a Digital 
channel partner.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
