Sandy McLaughlin
(508) 264-7981


       ...Integrated Networking, Extensive Desktop Management...


             DIGITAL ANNOUNCES CELEBRIS GL: DESKTOP PCs
          THAT OPTIMIZE WINDOWS 95 FOR ENTERPRISE COMPUTING


     ...Answers Customer Demand for All-Encompassing Desktop PC...


MAYNARD, Mass., Aug. 21, 1995  Digital Equipment Corporation today 
announced the Celebris GL family of high-performance desktop PCs 
that feature board-level integration of top-line audio, video and 
networking - unavailable in any other system in its price class - 
making the Celebris GL an ideal and highly affordable Windows 95 
client. 

     The Celebris GL PCs offer advanced business users a potent 
combination of performance, flexibility and ease-of-use, 
incorporating powerful Intel Pentium processors and the latest 
multimedia, graphics and communications technologies, as well as 
enhanced DMI network management, backed by uncompromising system 
hardware.  The systems, which are available in low-profile and 
short-tower configurations, will begin shipping on August 24, 1995, 
the day the new Windows 95 operating system is released.

     "The Celebris GL family is the first product launched since 
Digital and Microsoft announced on August 2 a strategic alliance to 
meet customer demand for solutions and support in enterprise-wide 
computing," said Enrico Pesatori, vice president and general manager 
of Digitals Computer Systems Division. "The Celebris GL family gives 
business users the best of both world's Microsoft's leadership in 
client/server software, and Digital's leadership in PC clients, 
service, networking connectivity and systems integration."

Rock-Solid Technology for Demanding Applications 

     Celebris GL systems provide integrated technology that is ideal 
for fast-response, demanding business and analytical applications 
such as 3D illustration, financial and scientific analysis and video 
conferencing.  Systems incorporate high-performance hardware 
components:  Pentium processors; EDO memory; pipeline burst cache; 
Intel Triton FX chipset; PCI bus master Enhanced-IDE and integrated, 
extended performance 64-bit graphics.  

     Workstation-quality multimedia technology - integrated at 
system level - includes a Matrox MGA Millennium graphics controller 
that offers high-performance 2D/3D graphics acceleration.  Dual 
ported 2MB WRAM graphics memory (upgradeable to 8MB), provides 
true-color graphics and high-resolution display.  High-quality 
16-bit stereo sound and quad-speed CD-ROM for fast response are 
included on every preconfigured model.  

     Digital also is integrating its industry-leading PCI Ethernet 
controller, offering users two connectivity options for maximum 
network compatibility, and an Easy Network Setup utility in every 
Celebris GL system, as well as bundling Spry Internet browsing 
software for LANs.

     "In designing the Celebris GL systems, we asked corporate 
customers what they really wanted in a high-performance desktop PC, 
and delivered it," said Howard Elias, vice president, Desktop 
Product Line for Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit.  
"In todays business environment, where system management and 
maintenance can make up 75 percent of computing costs, the Celebris 
GL system captures the sweet spot of enterprise computing, with 
powerful technology that requires less time and expense to install, 
use and manage." 

Extended Desktop Management Lowers Cost of Ownership

     Celebris GL systems exploit Digitals renowned networking 
expertise, expanding on the company's superior Desktop Management 
Interface (DMI), already implemented in the Venturis Pentium line 
and soon to be made available for all Digital desktop products.  
Celebris GL offers an enhanced DMI service layer and a unique 
software extension to Microsoft's Systems Management Server.

     For administrators in networked, enterprise environments, 
Celebris GL systems with the enhanced DMI service layer provide 
superior manageability, improved asset management, ease of 
installation and faster deployment for standalone and LAN-based PCs.  
The new capabilities reduce cost of ownership, save time, training 
and travel costs, and improve response time, all resulting in higher 
user productivity and satisfaction.

     Along with remote configuration/diagnostics, management and 
troubleshooting, the Celebris GL is designed to communicate a wealth 
of new information, including chassis serial number, and actively 
instrumented fields including motherboard serial number, CPU speed, 
model name, memory installed, and BIOS revision to popular 
enterprise and workgroup management tools including Microsoft System 
Management Server, Digital POLYCENTER AssetWORKS, and Intel LANDesk 
Management Suite 2.01, and others.

     As part of its relationship with Microsoft, Digital has 
developed a software extension to Microsoft System Management Server 
for all Digital desktop PC products, enabling System Management 
Server to read DMI information, and allow network administrators to 
report and display more data about their network than is available 
with other manufacturers PCs.

The Ideal Windows 95 Client

     Celebris GL incorporates multiple features that optimize the 
Windows 95 experience for desktop users.  Plug and Play, DMI client 
support and Windows 95 shutdown software augment setup and 
management.  Digital's integrated PCI Ethernet and Easy Network 
Setup utility optimize Windows 95s specifications for efficient, 
integrated networking.  In addition, a specially designed keyboard 
for Windows 95 and Windows 95 "getting started" software provide 
easy adaptability.

     Digital's worldwide service and support organization includes 
the largest number of Microsoft-certified professionals available to 
help users prepare for and make the transition to Windows 95.  
A Worldwide Microsoft Authorized Support Center partner, Digital has 
extensive Microsoft product knowledge, and Microsoft has selected 
Digital for the Launch Support Team of Windows 95 in the US and 
Europe, and for the Enterprise Migration Program, which assists 
resellers in successfully migrating corporate customers to Windows 
95 and Microsoft Office for Windows 95.

     Celebris GL features a dual-install strategy for Windows 95 and 
Windows for Workgroups 3.11/DOS operating systems and supports 
Windows NT Workstation, OS/2 and SCO UNIX/ODT operating systems.  
Systems are equipped with "Digital's Getting Started" user 
interface, as well as Plug and Play, QA Plus Pro Diagnostics and 
Adobe Acrobat Reader 2.0 software.

     Systems are available with 90MHz, 100MHz, 120MHz and 133MHz 
models in both low profile and short tower configurations.  Celebris 
GL short tower configurations provide an on-board Adaptec PCI SCSI 
chip, leaving the five slots and six bays free, maximizing system 
configuration options for unparalleled expansion capability.  

     Prices range from $2,799 for the Celebris GL 590 to $4,299 for 
a Celebris GL 5133ST model.  As with all Digital systems, Celebris 
GL is backed by a three-year limited hardware warranty, including 
one year on-site, and Digital's unmatched worldwide services and 
support network.  Digital was one of the few vendors to be ranked in 
the "A" category for PC desktop service and reliability by a survey 
of PC Magazine readers published in the July issue.  

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Intel and Alpha 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in todays global marketplace.
