Digital Broadens Range of Pentium Solutions for General Business Users
    
     Digital's Venturis line, designed for today's personal computing
business needs, offers ease of installation and use for general
business environments. The company noted that it has begun volume
shipments of the Venturis 5120, announced earlier this summer, and
introduced new models to the line based on Intel's fastest chip to date
-- the Pentium 133MHz processor. The new Venturis 5133 brings a higher
level of power and performance to the Venturis family, utilizing
high-performance, 64-bit accelerated PCI local bus graphics and a
dual-channel Enhanced-IDE interface. Graphics-intensive applications
benefit from the system's 1MB of standard graphics memory, upgradeable
to 2MB. The Venturis 5120 is priced from U.S. $2,199,-$2,599 and the
new Venturis 5133 models range from U.S. $2,449 to $2,849.
    
Digital's Entire Notebook and Desktop Product Lines to Sport 
Windows 95 Logo
    
     Digital said that all currently shipping notebooks and commercial
and retail desktops, which number more than 50 models, have been fully
tested by Microsoft and are certified to wear the Windows 95 logo. 
According to Microsoft no other company has as many models currently
certified to run with Windows 95.

     Earlier this week, Digital also cut prices on its industry- leading
HiNote and HiNote Ultra notebook products, with reductions ranging from
14 to 30 percent. Today's pricing actions do not impact the company's
new Starion retail desktop products, announced earlier this week, that
optimize Windows 95 for the general consumer market and include the
industry's first PC models with "home-theater-quality" sound. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated worldwide
information systems. Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, storage,
networking, software and services, together with industry-focused
solutions from business partners, help organizations compete and win in
today's global marketplace. 
