                DIGITAL DELIVERS FULL DCE SECURE-CORE
                    IMPLEMENTATION ON WINDOWS NT


       ...Version 1.1 to ship on Alpha and Intel platforms...


BOSTON, Mass. -- August 22, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
announced today at the OSF DCE Developer's Conference that it will 
deliver the full secure-core of OSF's Distributed Computing 
Environment (DCE) for Windows NT on both the Alpha and Intel 
platforms.  Version 1.1 of Digital's DCE provides application 
developers with the full complement of the tools needed to develop 
fully secure enterprise-wide applications on Windows NT platforms.  

     Digital's DCE includes four separate products: DCE Security 
Server,  DCE Cell Directory Server, DCE Runtime Services and DCE 
Application Developer's Kit.  The DCE Security Server provides 
authentication and authorization services for network applications, 
enhancing the level of protection for sensitive enterprise 
solutions.  The DCE Cell Directory Server provides the ability to 
contact people, locate resources, print queues and servers without 
needing to know their physical location.

     "Digital is pleased to be a leader in providing customers with 
the DCE  products they need for building secure applications across 
a mix of Windows NT, OpenVMS, and Digital UNIX platforms," said 
Gerard van de Aast, Digital's vice president, Enterprise Software 
Group. "With this announcement, we now offer the tools for developing 
a complete enterprise computing solution from the desktop through 
application servers to production servers."

Integration with Windows NT Enhances Performance

     For enhanced performance, Digital's DCE V1.1 products are fully 
integrated with the Windows NT operating system using the Microsoft 
Remote Procedure Call communication mechanism available in Windows 
NT, as well as native 32-bit threads.  An integrated login 
capability allows customers to use one password to log into both 
Windows NT and DCE. 

     "This is the product upon which I would bet my business," said 
Alan Jamison, software engineer at Open Environment Corporation.  
"Windows NT will become one of the most important DCE platforms, and 
Digital's implementation is my choice for critical DCE projects."

     Included with Digital's DCE Runtime Services for Windows NT is 
the DCE  Director, a graphical task-oriented DCE administration tool 
that eliminates the need to remember and type cumbersome commands to 
perform common DCE management functions.  "The DCE Director is 
especially useful and decreases the complexity of administration and 
management in a user friendly way," noted Neil Frasur, consultant at 
Curriculum Corp.

Application Developers' Kit Incorporates Advancements 
from R1.1 and R1.2.1 releases

     Digital's DCE for Windows NT products are based on the R1.0.3 
DCE source code from the OSF.  Digital has upgraded the Windows NT 
DCE Application Developer's Kit with features from the R1.1 and  
R1.2.1 OSF releases. The Application Developer's Kit includes an 
R1.2.1 enhancement that allows developers to create DCE applications 
in C++ that support distributed objects.  The product also contains 
the Generic Security Service Application Programming Interface (GSSAPI) 
from OSF R1.1 DCE release.  The GSSAPI provides security services to 
distributed applications that use peer-to-peer communication instead 
of DCE Remote Procedure Calls. 

     Digital has been shipping DCE Runtime services for Windows NT 
desktops since September 1994, on both Intel and Alpha platforms.  
Digital also offers DCE products on Digital UNIX (Alpha) and OpenVMS 
(Alpha and VAX). 

     Digital DCE for Windows NT V1.1 will be available on Sept. 21, 
1995.  The  Runtime Services are priced at $95; the Software 
Developer's Kit is priced at  $332; the Cell Directory Server is 
priced at $1,500; and the Security Server is priced at $1,500.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
