            FRANK P. DOYLE ELECTED TO BOARD OF DIRECTORS
                  OF DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION
                                  

MAYNARD, Mass. -- August 24, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
(NYSE:DEC) today announced the election of Frank P. Doyle to the 
company's Board of Directors, effective immediately.

     Doyle, 64, is executive vice president at General Electric 
Company (GE) and a member of its three-person corporate executive 
office.  Prior to this assignment, he was senior vice president of 
GE with responsibility for industrial relations, government 
relations, public relations, marketing communications and automotive 
industry sales.  Before joining GE in 1978, he held a series of 
increasingly responsible staff and operations positions at 
Curtiss-Wright Corporation, American Standard Corporation, Western 
Union and Pan American World Airways.  He currently serves on the 
Board of Directors of Paine Webber Group, Inc. and on the Board of 
the Educational Testing Service in Princeton, New Jersey.

     Doyle chaired the Committee for Economic Development's study on 
Work and Change, was a member of the US Secretary of Labor's Task 
Force on Worker Dislocation and, in 1992, was elected director of 
the National Academy of Human Resources.  He received his bachelor 
of arts degree from the University of Notre Dame and his MBA from 
Rutgers University.

     In announcing this election, Digital Chairman Robert B. Palmer 
said, "Frank Doyle is a recognized national leader in all areas of 
human resources and a seasoned senior manager of one of the most 
respected companies in the world.  We are pleased to have him join 
our Board of Directors, and we are confident that he will make 
significant contributions to Digital."

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
