                "SURF'S-UP" AT DIGITAL PC HOME PAGE


                  PC Business Unit Unveils Dynamic
               Interactive Home Page; Celebrates with
          Quarterly Drawings for HiNote Notebook Computers


MAYNARD, Mass., Aug. 29, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the formal launch of its Digital PC home page on 
the Internet, designed for prospective customers, key partners, and 
users and resellers of the company's PC products around the world.   
Exploiting the latest interactive technology, the Digital PC
World Wide Web site at http://www.pc.digital.com is fast, easy to 
navigate and highly intuitive. 

     At the Digital PC home page, users can navigate the site and 
step into the wider world of interactivity as easily as stepping 
into their own backyards.  A magazine-like format features vivid 
graphics and logical, intuitive text for obtaining late-breaking 
news and product information, customer service and support, free 
software device driver updates and details about purchasing
Digital PCs.  The Digital PC home page also includes a variety of 
"HotLinks" to additional Digital Web sites, partner sites and other 
useful resources at several popular Web sites on the Internet.

     Digital will celebrate the unveiling of its new Web site with 
quarterly drawings, offering a Digital HiNote notebook computer to 
lucky site visitors* randomly chosen from those who register in the 
home page's online "Guest Book."  Visitors can also sign up to 
participate in future online electronic surveys, enabling Digital 
to conduct "just-in-time" customer and market research.  The 
company plans to offer a variety of other contests in the future
and activities of interest to the broad range of Digital PC users 
visiting the company's Web site.

     "The Digital PC home page is a natural evolution from our 
pioneering efforts on the Internet and long history of networking 
expertise -- as well as our strength in the PC market," said 
Stephan A. Gray, vice president of communications and marketing 
services for Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit.  "Digital 
has created a hub of information and activity for PC users that
starts with the familiarity of a neighborhood but extends to the 
far-reaching corners of the world."

Five Key Sections Facilitate "Smooth Surfing" for PC-Related 
Information

     The Digital PC home page includes five main areas for fast, 
simple navigation and useful, extensive PC information available 24 
hours a day, seven days a week.  Visitors can click on a variety of 
topics, updated regularly, to obtain all the latest information on 
Digital's personal computer products, services, promotions, 
partnerships and even career opportunities:
       
     o Newswire:  Highlights breaking news about key partnerships    
       and Digital's full line of personal computer products and        
       services with an easy-to-use news index.  The section also        
       includes current press coverage about Digital PCs --        
       commercial and retail desktops, mobile computers, and PC 
       servers -- such as product reviews and announcements of new 
       offerings.

     o Products:  Includes background information on Digital's       
       entire range of personal computer products and details on     
       all the latest developments within Digital's PC lines.
       For example, press releases and system specifications for 
       the company's recently introduced Celebris GL and Starion 
       lines of out-of-box, Internet-ready commercial and retail 
       desktops can be found in this section. 

     o Customer Support:  Provides customers with the location of 
       service centers, warranty information, reference documents     
       such as background papers, and an opportunity to offer 
       feedback  on Digital's service and support programs.

     o PC Sales:  Supplies customers with a listing of where to buy 
       Digital PCs, including retail locations in the United        
       States, U.S. government resellers and additional resellers        
       worldwide.  

     o Employment:  Lists current job opportunities within 
       Digital's PC Business Unit, qualifications required and 
       details about how interested parties can obtain additional 
       information or send their resumes online via the Internet to 
       apply for these positions.

Catch a "Hyper-Wave" to Other Popular Destinations

     In addition to helping visitors find Digital PC-specific 
information, the new home page includes a sixth key area called 
"HotLinks."   HotLinks provides speedy access to related points of 
interest such as other Digital Web Sites, where visitors can "surf" 
for financial and investor information as well as instructions for 
ordering Digital solutions online; partner sites, such as 
Microsoft's new Windows 95 Internet home page or Intel's home page; 
or instantly link to a variety of entertainment, business and trade 
sites.  Following is a brief summary of HotLinks highlights: 

     o Digital Sites:  Including the company's Corporate, Windows 
       NT, Customer Service and Internet home pages.

     o Partner Sites:  Ranging from Microsoft and Intel to 
       Avnet/Hallmark Computers and Pioneer-Standard Electronic.

     o Other Useful Resources:  Including sites for navigating the 
       Internet such as NYNEX Interactive Yellow Pages, Netsurfer 
       and Yahoo; travel and business home pages like TravelWeb and 
       Ticketmaster; news and information services such as 
       NewsPage and USA Today; and sports and gaming sites like the 
       1996 Olympics and Sega.

Powered by Prioris

     High-powered servers are the foundation of any successful home 
page, ensuring uninterrupted access for a large number of users.  
The new Digital PC home page is powered by Digital Prioris HX 590DP 
PC servers, the same servers supporting Microsoft's Windows 
Launch95 Web site and last week's online event on August 24.

     "Being selected by the world's largest software company to 
help launch the greatest event in Internet history proves that 
Digital's Prioris servers are helping to propel the online wave," 
said Duane Dickhut, vice president, PC server product line for 
Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit.  "When combined with 
software from our partners, Prioris servers are an ideal Internet 
platform."

     The Prioris HX 590DP is a highly acclaimed departmental 
application server for workgroups numbering in the hundreds, 
delivering excellent reliability and fault-tolerant features.  
Optimized to meet customers' processor, disk and memory scalability 
needs, the Prioris HX 590 is specifically designed for expansion, 
growth and longevity.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
				####

*    Site visitors from states or other locations where such a 
     giveaway is prohibited by law are not eligible for the 
     drawing.

