              DIGITAL ANNOUNCES INTERNET ALPHASERVER
                       SOFTWARE KIT FOR UNIX


        Integrated, Ready To Use Suite of Internet Software
                         in prepackaged kit


MAYNARD, MA--August 3, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that the Internet AlphaServer Software Kit is now 
available as a separately orderable, prepackaged, kit for the 
entire Digital UNIX Alpha platform.  This enabling software runs on 
all AlphaServer or AlphaStation systems from the entry-level 200, 
to the widely popular 2100 price/performance leader, through 
Digital's mainframe/supercomputing 8000 series.  

     "Our customers are experiencing tremendous growth and need 
Internet applications without changing server platforms," said Rose 
Ann Giordano, vice president of Digital's Internet Business Group.  
"We created the Software Kit in response to our customers' and 
partners' request for scalability in building and supporting 
Internet solutions on all of Digital's AlphaServers."

     The Internet AlphaServer software previously was sold only 
prepackaged with the Internet Alpha Server Systems family.  With 
this announcement, now all of Digital's UNIX Alpha systems can be 
made application ready for Internet use. 

     This pretested Internet Software Kit contains the following:  

     o ELECTRONIC LOCKER system administration software allows 	   
       users to easily manage their server and user accounts with a 
       Mosaic-like interface.  This software includes system 
       administration functions including managing user accounts,    
       server components and information using hypertext browsers    
       like Mosaic, and Netscape Navigator.  Routine tasks can be    
       performed with a simple point-and-click interface. 

     o The fully supported Netscape Communications Server, version 
       1.1 from Netscape Communications -  the 'hottest' Internet 
       communications software on the 'hottest' systems on the 
       market today. This product provides high  performance, 	   
       easy-to-use server software for publishing rich, hypertext    
       documents on the Internet's World Wide Web.  When combined    
       with Digital's Alpha platform, customers get superb 
       price/performance and functionality.

     o Includes freeWAIS, INN  Network News Server, Tin News 	   
       Reader, CERN World Wide Web server software, Pine Mail and  
       LYNX - the most popular public Internet applications. 

     o MailWorks for Digital UNIX -  combines the reliability and
       security of host-based mail systems with the flexibility and
       ease of use of PC LAN mail systems, resulting in better     
       services at lower cost. (This product is licensed 	   
       separately.)

     The kit utilizes the Telnet and FTP Internet Applications 
supplied by Digital UNIX.  A POP3 mail server is also available as 
a part of Digital UNIX Operating System. A complete range of 
software support, planning, design, implementation and maintenance 
services is available as an option with this product.  
Comprehensive security Firewall services are also available.

     The Software Kit, integrated with the industry leading 
performance of Digital's 64 bit AlphaServer family and with the 
award winning, standards-compliant Digital UNIX operating system, 
creates a server that is ideal for providing the multimedia 
capability that today's customers demand. The scalability of Alpha 
systems allows Internet application developers to select a system 
for their current needs and and still have the option to expand and 
grow in the future.

     For customer convenience the Kit is also available prepackaged 
with the newly revised Internet AlphaServer family announced July 
26th.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry 
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations 
compete and win in today's global marketplace.
