             DIGITAL SHOWCASES WORLD'S FASTEST GRAPHICS
                    WORKSTATIONS AT SIGGRAPH '95


Siggraph '95, Los Angeles, CA, August 8, 1995 -- At Siggraph '95, 
Digital is showing its newly announced AlphaStation 600, which 
shatters all major workstation performance records, and new ZLXp-L 
series graphics adapters and Freedom Series graphics subsystems from 
Evans & Sutherland. Siggraph '95 -- the world's largest and most 
prestigious conference and exhibition on computer graphics and 
interactive techniques -- begins today in the Los Angeles Convention 
Center. 

New Multimedia Solutions

     Today Digital is also expanding its portfolio of multimedia 
solutions with new applications requested by users. These include: 

     o 	IconAuthor 6.0 for UNIX/Alpha and Windows NT/Alpha from 
        AimTech Corporation -- the first full-featured multimedia 
        authoring tool available for Alpha platforms.
 
     o 	Speech recognition software developed jointly by Digital 
     	and Dragon Systems -- the first commercial software for 
        workstations with continuous speech recognition capability.

     o 	Razor Pro for NT -- video editing software from In: Sync 
        that gives anyone working with video data unsurpassed 
        workstation speed and performance and reduces production 
        time for both video and film projects.

     o 	Open Inventor, a 3D object-oriented toolkit from Portable 
        Graphics, Inc. -- products that simplify and accelerate the 
        process of writing high-performance, interactive 3D 
        visualization and animation applications. 

     The theme of Digital's booth, "Performance Plus," features
demonstrations of the fastest graphics workstations in the world, 
plus a full range of tools and applications -- especially for visual 
simulation -- in target markets such as mechanical computer-aided 
design, architecture, engineering and construction, science and 
research, and more. 

     "Digital's exhibits at Siggraph '95 show users how they can 
increase their productivity with the applications they want on Alpha 
platforms at speeds they never thought possible," said Philippe 
Ribeyre, vice president of Digital's Workstations Business Segment. 
"Digital offers the widest range of graphics and multimedia 
solutions in the industry, running on the fastest workstations in 
the world -- AlphaStation 600 workstations with graphics 
accelerators from Digital and Evans & Sutherland." 

Champion Challenge Virtual Reality Demo

     Digital's "Champion Challenge Virtual Reality" demonstration 
shows off the power of AlphaStation workstations and Evans & 
Sutherland graphics options. Audience participants can to board one 
of two motorcycles and race against each other in a futuristic 
virtual reality Mayan racing event, navigating through a constantly 
changing course. This demo is powered by three AlphaStation 600 
workstations and Evans & Sutherland Freedom Series graphics 
subsystems. The audience watches the race on a large screen and can 
help introduce obstacles and barriers into the course.

Time Trial Spectacular Stage Show

     The "Time Trial Spectacular" theater uses the metaphor of 
racing to show users the superior performance of AlphaStations in 
four categories -- speed, graphics, multimedia, and system 
endurance. Featured in the superpower speedway are Digital's 
two-year application performance lead with 64-bit AlphaStations 
against 32-bit "jalopies" from Sun Microsystems and Hewlett-Packard 
and 64-bit workstation first-timer SGI; "high-octane" graphics from 
Digital and Evans & Sutherland; multimedia "Moto-Cross," where users 
don't have to waste time wallowing alone, spinning their wheels
when they can work as part of a team; and system endurance, showing
Digital's three-year warranty and 12- to 18-month lead in processor
performance as a marathon lifecycle. One audience member at each 
performance will win stock car driving lessons at the famed 
DriveTech Racing School. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
