||||||  Digital Press and Analysts News  ||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||
                                              Digital Equipment Corporation
                                          Maynard, Massachusetts 01754-2571


                    DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION

                             FACT SHEET


THE DIGITAL - MICROSOFT PARTNERSHIP

For more than ten years, Digital Service has been a key provider of 
support and training on a broad range of Microsoft operating system 
and application products all over the world and has virtually every 
accreditation that Microsoft offers.

On August 2, 1995, Digital and Microsoft announced a strategic 
alliance to meet growing customer demand for Microsoft-based 
solutions and support in enterprise-wide computing.  The alliance 
combines Microsoft client/server products with Digital's leadership 
in enterprise systems, service, support and systems integration and 
enables customers to deploy business solutions on the Microsoft 
Windows and Windows NT operating systems with assurance of 
integration into the most complex business environments.

The new agreement also includes a commitment by Microsoft for 
products based on Digital's Alpha platform, Microsoft's licensing of 
Digital clustering technology for inclusion in future Microsoft 
clustering solutions for Windows NT, and funding by Microsoft in 
Digital's support and systems integration business focused on 
Microsoft-based solutions.

Digital has also been awarded a five-year exclusive contract to 
manage the worldwide client/server infrastructure for The Microsoft 
Network, Microsoft's forthcoming on-line services offering 
incorporated into Windows 95. Under that agreement Digital will 
manage the wide-area backbone network, the data center, and the help 
desk function for the environment that will support Microsoft's 
products and services.

Digital is also one of only four service providers authorized to 
provide worldwide support for Microsoft products. In addition, it 
maintains the largest Microsoft Training Center, and is a Large 
Account Reseller, Authorized Solutions Provider and Authorized 
Support Center for Microsoft.

During the initial months of peak support demand for Windows 95, 
Digital will join Microsoft in providing telephone support for 
customers who are in their initial 90-day period of no-charge 
support for Windows 95.  Digital support staff will have access to 
the same broad range of information and tools and will employ the 
same problem-escalation processes as Microsoft support engineers.
        
Digital was chosen by Microsoft as a Windows 95 launch partner for 
its ability to respond to customer needs as demonstrated by its 
strength in managing high-volume call centers, its facilities and 
telecommunications capabilities, and ability to adapt to changing 
needs with staffing and contingency planning.

In addition, Digital is a top service and support partner of 
numerous other networking and application solution providers in the 
industry, supporting more than 14,000 products from 1,300 vendors 
including Novell and Lotus.
                                ####

