                                              Digital Equipment Corporation
                                          Maynard, Massachusetts 01754-2571


                    DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION

                             FACT SHEET


PRODUCT NAME:   Technology Migration Services


OVERVIEW:

There is universal agreement that the key to successful migration to 
Microsoft's Windows 95 operating system is solid planning based on 
accurate, reliable data.  Migrating to the new software will create 
profound changes in the way desktop users work.  Obtaining the 
maximum benefit from the feature-rich operating system demands the 
right technology infrastructure, resolution of complex 
interoperability issues and proper training for MIS staff and 
end-users.

Before, during and after the migration to Windows 95, Digital 
Equipment Corporation offers customers a matchless suite of services 
that can be customized to meet the needs of companies, regardless of 
size and scale of operation.  Digital service experts can work with 
corporate IT staffs and end-users to determine whether, when and how 
to make the move to Windows 95.

Before migration, Digital services assist companies in determining 
the impact Windows 95 will have on their people, organizations and 
support functions.  During the actual migration, Digital's support 
offerings reduce implementation costs, accelerating time-to-results, 
and enable key customer resources to focus on critical activities.  
Once the migration is completed, Digital can provide the ongoing, 
day-to-day support services required to maintain the new computing 
environment.
       
Specific Technology Migration Services

    *  Assessment of the impact of Windows 95 migration.
    *  Definition of hardware, software and network requirements.
    *  Development of a sound migration strategy and solid 
       implementation plan.
    *  Training for technical support staff and end-users.
    *  PC Utility and Software Utility contracts.
    *  Software asset management.
    *  Upgrading current desktop equipment
    *  Reconfiguration and optimization of networks.
    *  Customized help desk support.
    *  Management and maintenance of the desktop environment for 
       peak day-to-day performance. 

Key competitive differentiators

Key competitive differentiators between Digital's service and 
support offerings for Windows 95 and those of other vendors span 
three crucial areas:  program/project management, portfolio of 
offerings, and the Digital/Microsoft relationship.

    *  Program/Project Management: Spanning all of Digital's 
       migration services is comprehensive program management that 
       insures all elements of the migration are coordinated and 
       cost-efficient. Single point-of-accountability and contact 
       make project coordination seamless and efficient. This 
       approach makes sure that the technology addresses the needs 
       of the users, not the other way around.  It is simply a 
       matter of focus but it yields superior results.
        
    *  Portfolio of Services: In creating its Technology Migration 
       Services, Digital has customized its proven and market-tested 
       service and support tools for Windows 95.  These robust 
       service and support offerings provide customers with 
       virtually everything they need to migrate quickly, 
       efficiently and with minimal disruption to day-to-day 
       operations. 

       Supporting complex multivendor environments has been a core 
       mission of Digital for more than a decade.  Unlike many 
       competitors now entering the burgeoning market, Digital has 
       developed and refined its offerings in some of the  most 
       sophisticated and demanding computing environments all over 
       the world.

       Digital's expertise in volume procurement and licensing, for 
       example, makes new hardware/software and upgrade acquisitions 
       simple and as inexpensive as possible. Sophisticated 
       interoperability testing and staging capabilities guarantee 
       trouble-free network reconfigurations and installations. For 
       large companies facing large-scale hardware upgrades or 
       replacements, Digital offerings such as PC Utility and 
       Software Utility provide flexible, cost-effective solutions. 
       Digital provides Microsoft Certified Systems Engineer 
       training and certification for customer technical staff. 
       End-user training comes in a variety of offerings, from 
       custom curricula to on- or off-site classes and multimedia 
       CDs.
        
       From initial assessment to technical consulting, post-
       migration training, ongoing support and product disposition 
       and disposal, Digital's Technology Migration Services offer 
       flexible, scalable capabilities that can be customized to 
       meet any customer requirement.

    *  The Digital/Microsoft relationship:  Digital has been a key 
       partner with Microsoft and a provider of support services and 
       training on a broad range of Microsoft's operating system and 
       application products all over the world for more than ten 
       years.  During that time, Digital has attained virtually 
       every accreditation that Microsoft offers and has more 
       Microsoft-certified service representatives worldwide than 
       any other service vendor.  

In addition to being a support partner for the initial launch of 
Windows 95, Digital was awarded an exclusive, five-year contract to 
manage the worldwide client/server infrastructure for The Microsoft 
Network, the forthcoming on-line service incorporated in Windows 95.

Pricing and Availability
        
Digital will initially focus on providing migration services to 
companies that have already made the decision to move to Windows 95, 
using its assessment tools to help customers determine the best 
approach to take. The company has selected five large companies for 
inclusion in Microsoft's "early adopter" program and another 50 for 
rapid migration once Windows 95 is shipping, following the initial 
demand for immediate migration.
        
Pricing for Technology Migration Services will range from $150 to 
$800 per desktop, depending on the readiness of systems for Windows 
95, the complexity of their network environment, and the amount of 
support and training each company requires.
                                ####

