                    DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION

                          APPLICATION BRIEF


DIGITAL'S WINDOWS 95 MIGRATION SERVICES 
FEATURE QUICK, COST EFFECTIVE COMPLETION


"Our initial experience with migrating Digital employees to Windows 
95 and preliminary assessments from our first projects with larger 
customers allowed us to test our migration tools, service offerings, 
methodology and assumptions as they apply to fairly large-scale 
migrations to Windows 95," said Digital Windows 95 Program Manager 
Deborah Nicholls.  We achieved these migrations at costs ranging 
from $150 per desktop for "Windows95-ready" environments to $800 per 
seat for more complex situations demanding hardware upgrades, 
interoperability factors and extensive training and support."

Industry estimates of the cost of services for Windows 95 are pegged 
at $14 billion in total, with some $6 billion of that for outsourced 
services.  Analysts further estimate that the cost of migration of 
Windows 95 (excluding hardware upgrade costs) could range as high as 
$1000.00 per desktop.

"Our studies indicate that Digital's Technology Migration Services 
effectively provide companies with something we call "the service 
bridge" during the migration process," Nicholls said.  "Companies 
traditionally move to new technology with the expectation of 
increased benefits at lower cost. Their actual experience is, at 
least in the initial period of the migration, that costs soar and 
the benefits are difficult to realize.  Our migration services can 
dramatically minimize the disruption to current operations and the 
cost of the migration while accelerating the time it takes to 
realize the benefits." 

A survey of large corporate customers conducted by Microsoft to 
document concerns and issues of users related to Windows 95 
indicates that  those users were most concerned about the cost of 
migration, the impact on their current environments and their 
ability to retain backward compatibility across their enterprises.

Digital's Technology Migration Services addresses each of those 
concerns. The initial assessment phase of the process exposes all of 
the costs associated with the migration from a lifecycle cost of 
ownership perspective, not just initial cost of procurement.  That 
assessment, coupled with the actual migration planning, anticipates 
the impact of the migration on operations, enabling IS managers to 
structure the process so as to minimize disruptions.  It also 
focuses on compatibility and interoperability issues, enabling 
resolution before the actual migration process takes place.

"Perhaps the most vital difference between our Windows 95 migration 
services and those of our competitors is our emphasis on the 
"service bridge" approach and the service tools we have customized 
to make navigating that gap as efficient as possible," Nicholls 
related.  "Our program management approach, our complete array of 
offerings and worldwide capabilities and our close working 
relationship with Microsoft provide our customers with unmatched 
support for whatever migration strategies they choose..

"Windows 95 contains robust features that will enable IS managers to 
regain management control of  computing across the enterprise while 
providing end users with what they require.  The Digital migration 
approach further assures that IS managers will be able to meet the 
particular needs of their supported end-users on an ongoing basis.

"Our Technology Migration Services allow our customers to take 
unique advantage of  the Windows 95 migration to set in place a 
process that will insure smoother ongoing operations, better cost 
controls and a methodology for future migrations," Nicholls 
concluded. "The accelerating pace of new technologies demands that 
companies respond quickly and without disrupting their mission-
critical operations. Digital Technology Migration Services provides 
the template for that permanent capability." 
                                ####
 
