          PATHWORKS NETWORKING SOFTWARE EMBRACES WINDOWS 95


 ...Users To Benefit From Seamless, Enterprise-Wide Integration...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- August 14, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the expansion of its PATHWORKS for DOS and Windows 
networking software to include support for Windows 95.  With the new 
component of the PATHWORKS client software, Windows 95 users will 
have seamless, enterprise-wide integration of their PCs into their 
existing PATHWORKS environment, and management capabilities across 
multivendor network-operating-systems.

     Developed as a completely 'protected mode' implementation, 
freeing conventional memory on the desktop for other applications, 
the Windows 95 component of the PATHWORKS for DOS and Windows client 
software provides a new implementation of the DECnet transport, as 
well as LAT, CTERM, and Telnet transport protocols.  This allows 
access to server and network resources over Ethernet, Token Ring, 
and FDDI networks.  It also offers a VT320 terminal emulator for 
host-based communications and the latest version of the Spyglass 
Mosaic browser for Internet access. 

     The new PATHWORKS component utilizes the Windows 95 user 
interface, simplifying installation and management.  Using the 
step-by-step Wizard paradigm, loading the PATHWORKS Windows 95 
component is fast and easy, with automatic configuration of the 
users' PC to run PATHWORKS.  The System Monitor feature of Windows 
95 reveals DECnet and LAT activity, and the Network Neighborhood 
function shows PATHWORKS server status.  In addition, PATHWORKS for 
DOS and Windows on-line documentation has been enhanced and 
converted to the Windows 95 user interface.

     Available on August 24, the Windows 95 component of the 
PATHWORKS client software requires a minimum 25Mhz Intel 80386DX 
system with 8MB RAM and 10MB of hard disk space available.  A 
Windows 95-supported network adapter and driver is required.

     Customers will immediately benefit from the expansion of 
PATHWORKS to embrace Windows 95.  "I need to integrate Windows 95 
PCs into our networking environment," said Ellis Merlin, manager of 
Information Systems at Ciba-Geigy's Agricultural Biotechnology 
Research Unit.  "PATHWORKS lets me do that easily."

     Existing PATHWORKS V5.1 users already are licensed to use the 
Windows 95 component.  Customers with Media and Documentation 
Distribution Service (MDDS) contracts automatically will receive the 
PATHWORKS client software for Windows 95 at no charge. Customers 
with PATHWORKS V5.1 client licenses who do not have the  MDDS 
service are licensed to use the Windows 95 component and can order 
the installation kit for $20.  Customers without PATHWORKS currently 
installed can purchase a PATHWORKS for DOS and Windows CCS license 
for $205 which includes the Windows 95 component and provides 
unlimited access to PATHWORKS servers.  Client software and server 
access may also be ordered by calling 1-800-DIGITAL. 

     PATHWORKS for DOS and Windows with support for Windows 95 is a 
member of Digital's PATHWORKS family of networking and network 
integration solutions for local and wide area networks. PATHWORKS 
integrates the broadest set of PC and server platforms with the 
leading network technologies and network operating systems. 
PATHWORKS solutions are available for all popular platforms, 
including DOS, Windows, Windows NT, Windows for Workgroups, NetWare, 
Macintosh, LAN Manager, UNIX, OpenVMS, OS/2 and now Windows 95.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
